From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:12:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Step 10: language check, runner fixes, language-aware story
 prompt; web app design

First live routing run (45 turns): routing solid (tool 42/42, argument
36/36, relay 36/36, language switching 12/12, guard 3/3), but only 5/15
non-English stories were written in the requested language; the
structure-only check had passed the rest.

Detection and test harness
- Add language_check (script ratio for non-Latin languages, English-word
  share for the rest) and wire it into check_passage, the batch runner,
  --rescore and the routing tests; tested on the real outputs
- Routing cases for non-English stories name their language
- Runner: remove the throwaway word before every repeat (case-insensitive),
  collapse tool calls listed twice (keep ids), record per-turn latency
- Runner: own snapshot table name (words_autotest_snapshot) and a merging
  restore that deletes nothing

Tuning change 1: language-aware story prompt (story_tool.py)
- For languages other than English the prompt opens with a language rule
  (the list holds English meanings to express in the language; no English
  words left in), ends with a final-check reminder, and omits the English
  tone example
- normalize_language maps names given in the language itself to English
  names; used in the prompt and the cache key
- English prompts are unchanged, pinned by SHA-256 in the tests
- Add tests/test_story_prompt_language.py (no database)

Web app design
- Add docs/WEB-APP-DESIGN.md: local demo web app with React + TypeScript,
  a FastAPI backend, the Langflow flow as the AI layer, login, per-user
  and per-language vocabulary; diagrams, API table, wireframes, testing
  and milestones

Docs: record results, findings, the before/after procedure and the
deferred story_prompt_builder.py drift in the test plan, CHANGELOG,
DEVELOPER-DIARY and IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE
